(BIOLOGY 101 - CELL THEORY AND PHOTOSYNTHESIS) Tj T*
(Cell theory states that all living organisms are made of one or more cells,) Tj T*
(that the cell is the basic unit of life, and that all cells come from other) Tj T*
(cells. Robert Hooke first observed cells in cork in 1665, while Antonie van) Tj T*
(Leeuwenhoek was the first to observe living single-celled organisms, which) Tj T*
(he called animalcules, using hand made microscopes.) Tj T*
(Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants, algae and some bacteria) Tj T*
(convert light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose. The overall) Tj T*
(equation is 6 CO2 + 6 H2O + light energy -> C6H12O6 + 6 O2. It takes place) Tj T*
(in the chloroplasts, which contain the green pigment chlorophyll.) Tj T*
(The light dependent reactions occur in the thylakoid membranes. Chlorophyll) Tj T*
(absorbs light and excites electrons, which travel through an electron) Tj T*
(transport chain. Water molecules are split to replace these electrons, a) Tj T*
(process called photolysis, releasing oxygen as a waste product. The energy) Tj T*
(is stored briefly in ATP and NADPH.) Tj T*
(The light independent reactions, also called the Calvin cycle, occur in the) Tj T*
(stroma. Using the ATP and NADPH produced in the light reactions, the enzyme) Tj T*
(RuBP carboxylase \(rubisco\) fixes carbon dioxide into a three carbon sugar) Tj T*
(that is eventually assembled into glucose. Glucose is then used in cellular) Tj T*
(respiration to power the work of the cell.) Tj T*
(Limiting factors control the rate of photosynthesis: light intensity, carbon) Tj T*
(dioxide concentration and temperature. When any one of these is in short) Tj T*
(supply it becomes the limiting factor, no matter how abundant the others are.) Tj T*
(Exam question: describe how a leaf is adapted for photosynthesis, naming the) Tj T*
(palisade mesophyll, the stomata and the guard cells, and explain how each) Tj T*
(structure increases the rate of the reaction.) Tj T*
